{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Ehyeh asher Ehyeh.</b> The first is a name, and the second is the explanation of the name — that is, My name is Ehyeh because I shall be and endure for all eternity without end, and because I shall be with them to redeem them from the burdens of Egypt. This name of being Yaakov transmitted to his sons, as it is written: 'ויהי יהוה עמכם והשיב אתכם' etc. — whoever brings you tidings of the redemption from Egypt in the language of being together with the tidings of the visitation, you shall believe his words. And so they did: when Moshe and Aharon came and invoked for them this name of being, immediately 'ויאמן העם כי פקד'."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:59.938316956Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}